  "proved": false,
  "argument": "A missed-root colouring of extras does not prove omega(pool(U)) <= |U|.  Two extras that miss the same D5 root can still kiss: 236960 kissing pairs share at least one root (287360 root-edge incidences).  An explicit pair is recorded under coloring.example_pair (inner product 14 <= 16).  Same-missed extras \u2014 those with the same full seed \u2014 are edgeless, but sharing a single root is weaker and is not a stable set.  A principal-root colouring (the unique missed root of largest inner product, when it exists) does not cover the graph: only 640 extras have a unique principal root (the 640 type-B points); the 800 type-A and type-C extras have a tie, and 0 kissing pairs among the type-B points share a principal root. A tight star 8-clique on e0- has missed-set rank 5 over Q and 4 over GF(2), so the characteristic vectors are dependent and do not force |E| <= |U|.  Hall matching of a clique into U is equivalent to the inequality itself, not a separate reason.  The tests below found no U with omega > |U|, but that is a finite sample (plus the ten stars and every single seed), not a proof for every U.  Leftover |U| >= 19 of the 1480-graph remains open.  This does not claim tau_5 = 40.",
